  "title": "What each state gives the federal government and gets back, by IRS gross collections against USASpending award spending",
  "source": "IRS Statistics of Income, SOI Data Book Table 5, Gross Collections by Type of Tax and State (vintage discovered per run); USASpending.gov spending_by_geography, place of performance basis, same fiscal year window as the IRS vintage",
  "units": {
   "give_b": "federal tax gross collections, $ billions",
   "get_b": "federal award spending, $ billions",
   "pop": "population (from USASpending)",
   "give_pc": "give_b per person, $",
   "get_pc": "get_b per person, $ (USASpending's own per_capita figure)",
   "balance_b": "get_b minus give_b, $ billions",
   "balance_pc": "get_pc minus give_pc, $ per person",
   "ratio": "get_b / give_b"
  },
  "fields": {
   "code": "two-letter postal code",
   "is_state": "true ONLY for the 50 actual states; false for DC (excluded from the colour-scale domain) and for territories",
   "in_grid": "whether the jurisdiction is drawn on the tile-grid cartogram (states + DC only)"
  },
  "notes": [
   "THIS IS NOT A BALANCE OF PAYMENTS. Give is gross collections classified by the filer's address (IRS Table 5's own note); get is award spending classified by place of PERFORMANCE, not the recipient's residence. A border employer's withholding can be booked to a neighbouring state; a military base or federal retiree's former duty station pulls spending away from where the money is actually used. State this in body copy, never a tooltip.",
   "Award spending EXCLUDES most direct benefit payments (Social Security, Medicare, SNAP), so the \"get\" side understates what a state actually receives. Gross collections include penalties and interest and exclude excise taxes collected by Customs and the Alcohol and Tobacco Tax and Trade Bureau.",
   "DC is not a state, is an extreme outlier by construction (federal employment concentration), and is excluded from the colour-scale domain so it does not flatten the 50-state range. It is still drawn and still in the table.",
   "Territories (PR, GU, VI, MP, AS) appear in USASpending but not in IRS Table 5's state breakdown; give_b is null for them, not zero. They are not drawn on the tile grid.",
   "The Rockefeller Institute publishes an actual state balance-of-payments study; its series ends FY2022 and it is cited, never ingested (no machine-readable feed exists)."
  ],
